1
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:12,067
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,767 --> 00:00:32,733
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:35,267
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:40,033 --> 00:00:41,300
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,367 --> 00:00:44,167
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:44,167 --> 00:00:45,333
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,333 --> 00:00:46,467
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,767 --> 00:00:48,433
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,333 --> 00:00:51,333
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,667 --> 00:00:53,767
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:53,767 --> 00:00:55,433
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,667 --> 00:00:58,100
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,100 --> 00:01:00,400
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:01,167 --> 00:01:02,767
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,333 --> 00:01:06,433
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:09,433
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,233 --> 00:01:11,833
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,833 --> 00:01:13,200
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:14,700
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:20,133 --> 00:01:24,833
<i>I will do everything
to get out of this hellscape.</i>

21
00:01:24,833 --> 00:01:27,333
<i> I finally got Rudy to sign.</i>

22
00:01:27,333 --> 00:01:28,800
<i> I've got proof.</i>

23
00:01:28,800 --> 00:01:30,533
<i>For the price
of one million pesos,</i>

24
00:01:30,533 --> 00:01:32,633
she's willing to offer her soul.

25
00:01:32,633 --> 00:01:33,867
<i> Any news from the NLEA?</i>

26
00:01:33,867 --> 00:01:35,567
<i> Haven't they caught Gabo yet?</i>

27
00:01:35,567 --> 00:01:36,600
<i> Not yet.</i>

28
00:01:38,567 --> 00:01:39,633
<i> You're leaving already?</i>

29
00:01:39,633 --> 00:01:41,700
<i>I'm heading out to look
for a job.</i>

30
00:01:41,733 --> 00:01:43,433
<i> You need to look presentable.</i>

31
00:01:43,433 --> 00:01:44,767
<i> You need to get a haircut.</i>

32
00:01:44,767 --> 00:01:46,433
<i>I might lose my strength.
This is my source of power.</i>

33
00:01:46,433 --> 00:01:48,800
<i>And my sex appeal
looks better like this.</i>

34
00:01:53,067 --> 00:01:54,667
- [ISOBEL CRYING]
- [SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

35
00:01:54,667 --> 00:01:56,767
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

36
00:01:56,767 --> 00:01:58,067
- [TWINKLE] Ma'am?
- [INHALES DEEPLY]

37
00:02:01,067 --> 00:02:02,533
Ma'am, here's your breakfast.

38
00:02:03,033 --> 00:02:05,500
Toto, hurry up. Put it there.

39
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:07,000
- [PLATE CLATTERS]
- [CRYING]

40
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:08,000
Ma'am....

41
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:09,667
At least have
some coffee, ma'am.

42
00:02:09,667 --> 00:02:11,533
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

43
00:02:11,533 --> 00:02:15,467
I want you to put all
of Sam's pictures on display.

44
00:02:17,033 --> 00:02:19,900
All the beautiful photos
of my youngest

45
00:02:19,900 --> 00:02:21,533
where she looked like an angel.

46
00:02:21,933 --> 00:02:23,733
Display them all.

47
00:02:24,100 --> 00:02:28,000
Ma'am, the NCIA uniform
of Ma'am Sam...

48
00:02:28,467 --> 00:02:29,767
It's ready.

49
00:02:29,767 --> 00:02:34,700
And the setup here will be
started right away, ma'am.

50
00:02:34,700 --> 00:02:36,500
They said it'll be quick.

51
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:39,800
As quick as a person's life?

52
00:02:39,800 --> 00:02:45,033
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

53
00:02:49,067 --> 00:02:50,600
Why do I even need a haircut?

54
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:52,500
I'm just applying for a job.

55
00:02:52,500 --> 00:02:54,567
It's important.

56
00:02:54,567 --> 00:02:57,067
- [DANTE] Jeez.
- [MAMENG] Oh, Gabo...

57
00:02:57,067 --> 00:02:59,933
That's right, go get a haircut.

58
00:02:59,933 --> 00:03:02,767
Don't give Gloria
any more problems.

59
00:03:02,767 --> 00:03:04,667
[LIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]

60
00:03:04,667 --> 00:03:06,100
Okay, you win.
I'll get a haircut.

61
00:03:06,100 --> 00:03:07,233
What kind should I get?

62
00:03:07,233 --> 00:03:09,800
You know the popular style
these days?

63
00:03:09,800 --> 00:03:11,967
Buzz cut,
with sides shaved down and all.

64
00:03:11,967 --> 00:03:13,567
A gangster cut.

65
00:03:13,567 --> 00:03:14,500
Come on now.

66
00:03:14,500 --> 00:03:16,667
He's applying for a job!

67
00:03:16,667 --> 00:03:17,733
Listen, son.

68
00:03:17,733 --> 00:03:20,667
A clean young man's cut
looks better.

69
00:03:20,700 --> 00:03:23,100
A young man's cut, Papa?

70
00:03:24,767 --> 00:03:25,933
But I'm already married.

71
00:03:25,933 --> 00:03:27,767
Oh, yeah. That's right.

72
00:03:27,767 --> 00:03:28,833
He's got a point.

73
00:03:28,833 --> 00:03:32,167
[LIGHT MUSIC CONTINUES]

74
00:03:32,167 --> 00:03:33,200
I have an idea.

75
00:03:33,200 --> 00:03:36,100
Get a military cut.

76
00:03:36,100 --> 00:03:37,833
Tell that to the barber.

77
00:03:37,833 --> 00:03:40,033
Military cut? That's too high!

78
00:03:40,033 --> 00:03:42,167
My hair will be way too short.

79
00:03:42,167 --> 00:03:44,767
This is my source of power,
you know?

80
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:47,933
[CHUCKLES]
It'll be okay. Trust me.

81
00:03:47,933 --> 00:03:49,667
[LAUGHTER]

82
00:03:49,667 --> 00:03:52,167
[LIGHT MUSIC CONTINUES]

83
00:03:52,167 --> 00:03:54,700
Okay, just because I love you.

84
00:03:54,733 --> 00:03:57,533
[ALL SQUEALING, GIGGLING]

85
00:03:57,533 --> 00:03:59,667
- Gabo! Where are you going?
- [MAMENG] Let's head inside.

86
00:04:00,067 --> 00:04:02,233
To the barbershop, Miss Diday.

87
00:04:02,233 --> 00:04:04,000
- I'll pick out Gabo's clothes.
- You see, Gloria...

88
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:06,533
...wanted me to get a haircut
since I'm applying for a job.

89
00:04:06,800 --> 00:04:08,133
[KULAS]
Gabo, what's gotten into you?

90
00:04:08,133 --> 00:04:09,133
Getting a haircut?

91
00:04:09,133 --> 00:04:10,533
I really didn't want to.

92
00:04:10,533 --> 00:04:12,033
I'm worried how I'll look.

93
00:04:12,033 --> 00:04:14,567
[ESTONG] Oh, I just know
you'll feel weaker.

94
00:04:14,567 --> 00:04:15,967
That's what I kept saying
to them!

95
00:04:15,967 --> 00:04:17,533
I told them this is where
my power comes from.

96
00:04:17,533 --> 00:04:19,500
If I cut it, I might lose it.

97
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:21,300
If I didn't love Gloria,

98
00:04:21,300 --> 00:04:22,633
I wouldn't be taking her advice.

99
00:04:22,633 --> 00:04:23,667
[LIGHT MUSIC CONTINUES]

100
00:04:23,667 --> 00:04:25,500
[RUDY] Gloria.

101
00:04:25,567 --> 00:04:28,100
How did you convince Gabo
to get a haircut?

102
00:04:29,167 --> 00:04:31,233
Oh, it's simple.

103
00:04:31,233 --> 00:04:34,833
I just told him that he needs
to look professional.

104
00:04:34,833 --> 00:04:36,667
- He readily agreed.
- [MAMENG CHUCKLES]

105
00:04:36,667 --> 00:04:37,833
Gloria...

106
00:04:37,833 --> 00:04:38,900
Admit it.

107
00:04:38,900 --> 00:04:40,700
You pressured Gabo, didn't you?

108
00:04:40,700 --> 00:04:42,733
Psst! What's wrong with you?

109
00:04:42,733 --> 00:04:44,567
Don't listen to him, Gloria.
[CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

110
00:04:45,033 --> 00:04:48,167
It's good that Gabo listens
to you.

111
00:04:48,167 --> 00:04:49,533
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

112
00:04:49,533 --> 00:04:50,933
Ah, excuse me.

113
00:04:50,933 --> 00:04:53,833
I'll just go find clothes
for Gabo's interview tomorrow.

114
00:04:53,833 --> 00:04:55,833
- Sure thing, dear.
- Excuse me.

115
00:04:55,833 --> 00:04:57,100
[LIGHT MUSIC CONTINUES]

116
00:04:57,100 --> 00:04:58,667
Silly you!

117
00:04:58,667 --> 00:05:00,067
- Maybe she really forced him.
- You and your big mouth.

118
00:05:00,700 --> 00:05:03,333
[DIDAY] You really love Gloria,
don't you, Gabo?

119
00:05:03,367 --> 00:05:05,067
Absolutely, Miss Diday.

120
00:05:05,067 --> 00:05:07,733
[KULAS] A husband should
always listen to his wife.

121
00:05:07,733 --> 00:05:08,800
Of course!

122
00:05:08,800 --> 00:05:09,967
[KULAS] Whoa, hang on!

123
00:05:09,967 --> 00:05:11,733
I gave you a massage last night!

124
00:05:11,733 --> 00:05:13,033
Even scrubbed you!

125
00:05:13,033 --> 00:05:14,633
Sure, you did both.

126
00:05:14,633 --> 00:05:16,200
But you asked for payment!

127
00:05:16,200 --> 00:05:18,133
[ESTONG] Mama, Papa!
Cut it out, will you?

128
00:05:18,133 --> 00:05:20,800
The neighbors can hear you!
You're always bickering!

129
00:05:20,800 --> 00:05:22,633
I'm off to get a haircut now,
Miss Diday.

130
00:05:22,633 --> 00:05:23,867
[LIGHT MUSIC CONTINUES]

131
00:05:23,867 --> 00:05:24,833
[BOX SCRAPING]

132
00:05:29,933 --> 00:05:31,067
T-shirts.

133
00:05:31,067 --> 00:05:33,067
What's with his clothes?

134
00:05:38,067 --> 00:05:41,733
[LIGHT MUSIC CONTINUES]

135
00:05:41,733 --> 00:05:42,900
All casual.

136
00:05:43,300 --> 00:05:44,367
Let's check that box.

137
00:05:44,900 --> 00:05:45,867
[BOX SCRAPING]

138
00:05:47,067 --> 00:05:48,133
- [BOX THUDS]
- [SIGHS]

139
00:05:50,400 --> 00:05:52,300
What's up with all the jackets?

140
00:05:56,067 --> 00:05:57,067
This one.

141
00:05:58,167 --> 00:05:59,767
Doesn't he have other clothes?

142
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:01,767
I don't know what he could wear.

143
00:06:02,100 --> 00:06:04,100
None of these will work.

144
00:06:04,100 --> 00:06:08,767
[BOXES RUSTLING, SCRAPING]

145
00:06:11,433 --> 00:06:12,333
[MUSIC ENDS]

146
00:06:13,933 --> 00:06:14,933
[PHONE RINGING]

147
00:06:14,933 --> 00:06:16,167
Ma'am?

148
00:06:16,267 --> 00:06:18,767
Ma'am Isobel,
your phone's ringing.

149
00:06:20,200 --> 00:06:23,600
[RINGING CONTINUES]

150
00:06:24,300 --> 00:06:26,733
[BREATHES DEEPLY]

151
00:06:28,267 --> 00:06:29,800
Hello. Who's this?

152
00:06:31,967 --> 00:06:34,667
[MYSTERIOUS WOMAN]
<i> The person you need the most.</i>

153
00:06:34,667 --> 00:06:36,133
[MYSTICAL MUSIC PLAYING]

154
00:06:36,133 --> 00:06:37,267
Madam Rosa?

155
00:06:37,267 --> 00:06:38,933
Who else?

156
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:40,933
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

157
00:06:41,667 --> 00:06:43,100
Honestly...

158
00:06:44,133 --> 00:06:46,833
Sam is the one I need
the most right now.

159
00:06:48,133 --> 00:06:49,167
Sure.

160
00:06:50,167 --> 00:06:51,767
But, Isobel...

161
00:06:52,167 --> 00:06:55,067
Sam whispers to Madam Rosa

162
00:06:55,067 --> 00:06:58,267
the words she wants you to hear.

163
00:06:58,900 --> 00:07:02,967
So, are you available to speak
with your daughter today?

164
00:07:03,967 --> 00:07:05,933
Yes. I'm just at home.

165
00:07:06,467 --> 00:07:08,133
<i> Later today,</i>

166
00:07:08,133 --> 00:07:10,400
a memorial service
will be held for Sam.

167
00:07:10,400 --> 00:07:12,300
[MYSTICAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

168
00:07:12,300 --> 00:07:14,867
Wait for your daughter, Isobel.

169
00:07:15,733 --> 00:07:17,700
Madam Rosa will meet with you

170
00:07:17,700 --> 00:07:20,033
so you can speak with Sam.

171
00:07:20,033 --> 00:07:22,433
Alright, Madam Rosa.
I'll wait for you.

172
00:07:22,433 --> 00:07:23,967
I'll wait for you.

173
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:28,667
Yes! Exactly as planned!

174
00:07:29,100 --> 00:07:31,400
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

175
00:07:32,433 --> 00:07:39,400
[SORROWFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

176
00:07:48,300 --> 00:07:50,733
<i> - </i> [GUEST 1] <i> My condolences.
<i> - </i> [RICARDO]<i>   I appreciate it.</i></i>

177
00:07:50,733 --> 00:07:53,100
[GUEST 2]  Ricardo, we're sorry
for your loss.

178
00:07:53,100 --> 00:07:55,433
<i> - </i> [RICARDO]<i>   Thank you.
<i>-  [ISOBEL]    Thanks for comin.</i></i>

179
00:07:56,800 --> 00:07:58,467
[GUEST 1] <i> We sympathize
</i> with you, Isobel.

180
00:07:58,467 --> 00:08:05,400
[SORROWFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

181
00:08:20,133 --> 00:08:27,167
[SORROWFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

182
00:08:34,100 --> 00:08:41,100
[ISOBEL SOBBING]

183
00:08:43,067 --> 00:08:44,200
Sam...

184
00:08:45,500 --> 00:08:46,967
[BREATH QUIVERING]

185
00:08:46,967 --> 00:08:50,100
I wish this were just
a bad dream.

186
00:08:50,500 --> 00:08:53,133
I wish this weren't real.

187
00:08:53,900 --> 00:08:55,067
[INHALES DEEPLY]

188
00:08:55,100 --> 00:08:58,833
I can't imagine life
without you, sweetheart.

189
00:08:59,333 --> 00:09:02,500
[SOBBING CONTINUES]

190
00:09:02,500 --> 00:09:09,400
[SORROWFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

191
00:09:24,133 --> 00:09:28,433
[SORROWFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

192
00:09:28,467 --> 00:09:31,167
[PRIEST]
<i> Dear brothers and sisters,</i>

193
00:09:31,967 --> 00:09:34,133
<i> we are gathered here today</i>

194
00:09:34,633 --> 00:09:36,500
<i> to celebrate the life</i>

195
00:09:37,233 --> 00:09:41,333
of our dearly beloved Samantha.

196
00:09:41,633 --> 00:09:43,133
<i> The Lord gave,</i>

197
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,133
<i> and the Lord has taken away.</i>

198
00:09:47,133 --> 00:09:49,833
<i>In the name of the Lord,
we pray...</i>

199
00:09:49,833 --> 00:09:52,633
[SORROWFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

200
00:09:52,633 --> 00:09:56,600
<i>that eternal rest be granted
to Samantha...</i>

201
00:10:00,133 --> 00:10:03,133
<i>...and that perpetual light
shine upon her.</i>

202
00:10:04,233 --> 00:10:06,133
<i> May she rest in peace.</i>

203
00:10:07,167 --> 00:10:14,133
[SORROWFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

204
00:10:24,500 --> 00:10:28,233
[MAX]  I'll respect how Mom
and Dad are feeling.

205
00:10:29,233 --> 00:10:32,833
<i>But I refuse to believe that
Sam has passed away.</i>

206
00:10:33,500 --> 00:10:36,400
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

207
00:10:40,933 --> 00:10:41,900
[RICARDO] Uh...

208
00:10:43,133 --> 00:10:44,200
[RICARDO EXHALES]

209
00:10:46,200 --> 00:10:47,733
Samantha...

210
00:10:47,733 --> 00:10:50,133
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

211
00:10:50,133 --> 00:10:51,100
was, um...

212
00:10:52,300 --> 00:10:54,033
...our youngest child.

213
00:10:54,033 --> 00:10:55,567
[ISOBEL BREATHES DEEPLY]

214
00:10:58,200 --> 00:11:00,867
But I admit that, sometimes...

215
00:11:02,300 --> 00:11:06,700
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

216
00:11:06,700 --> 00:11:08,200
I haven't made her feel like...

217
00:11:09,800 --> 00:11:11,267
...I truly see her
as my daughter.

218
00:11:13,433 --> 00:11:19,000
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

219
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:21,133
She's always asking me
for a second chance.

220
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:23,233
And I didn't--

221
00:11:24,433 --> 00:11:26,633
I never listened to her.

222
00:11:28,267 --> 00:11:35,200
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

223
00:11:38,333 --> 00:11:39,300
Sam...

224
00:11:42,433 --> 00:11:43,367
I...

225
00:11:43,367 --> 00:11:44,333
[RICARDO SNIFFLES]

226
00:11:44,967 --> 00:11:46,667
I'm asking for a second chance.

227
00:11:47,800 --> 00:11:49,800
[ISOBEL CRYING SOFTLY]

228
00:11:49,800 --> 00:11:50,933
Just come back to us, Sam.

229
00:11:52,133 --> 00:11:53,767
Let me show you...

230
00:11:55,133 --> 00:11:56,100
[ISOBEL INHALES]

231
00:11:58,667 --> 00:11:59,767
...how much I love you.

232
00:12:04,967 --> 00:12:06,833
That I regret all...

233
00:12:10,100 --> 00:12:11,233
...of my shortcomings.

234
00:12:12,367 --> 00:12:13,833
Just come back, Sam.

235
00:12:14,800 --> 00:12:15,800
[ISOBEL INHALES SHAKILY]

236
00:12:18,133 --> 00:12:19,433
Daddy will make it up to you.

237
00:12:20,233 --> 00:12:21,200
[RICARDO SNIFFLES]

238
00:12:22,967 --> 00:12:23,933
I'll make it up to you.

239
00:12:24,700 --> 00:12:31,233
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

240
00:12:31,233 --> 00:12:32,267
I'm sorry.

241
00:12:34,800 --> 00:12:35,767
[ISOBEL INHALES SHAKILY]

242
00:12:38,333 --> 00:12:45,300
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

243
00:13:00,333 --> 00:13:07,333
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

244
00:13:12,267 --> 00:13:14,700
- [MAMENG] I'll have coffee.
- [SAM] Auntie?

245
00:13:15,767 --> 00:13:19,533
Auntie, do you have
some of Gabo's formal clothes?

246
00:13:19,533 --> 00:13:22,333
He'll need it
for his interview tomorrow.

247
00:13:22,367 --> 00:13:24,267
Oh, there's none.

248
00:13:24,267 --> 00:13:26,733
Gabo doesn't wear
that kind of thing.

249
00:13:27,133 --> 00:13:28,200
- Hey, Rudy.
- Hm?

250
00:13:28,200 --> 00:13:31,200
Maybe you have something
Gabo can borrow.

251
00:13:31,200 --> 00:13:32,233
Oh, I have nothing.

252
00:13:32,233 --> 00:13:34,833
If I did,
I might've thrown it away.

253
00:13:36,133 --> 00:13:37,367
[DANTE] Wait a second.

254
00:13:37,367 --> 00:13:39,467
Why don't you ask Diday?

255
00:13:39,467 --> 00:13:42,400
Her husband and her son
are both men.

256
00:13:42,400 --> 00:13:44,067
Maybe you can borrow from them.

257
00:13:44,067 --> 00:13:45,367
Okay, I'll give it a try.

258
00:13:48,200 --> 00:13:50,733
Gabo really has
no formal clothes.

259
00:13:51,433 --> 00:13:53,233
[SAM] Miss Diday! Miss Diday.

260
00:13:55,400 --> 00:13:58,567
Why are you acting
like we're not close?

261
00:13:58,567 --> 00:14:00,800
Just call me buddy
instead of Miss Diday!

262
00:14:00,800 --> 00:14:04,067
"Miss Diday" sounds like
I'm old.

263
00:14:04,067 --> 00:14:05,300
[KULAS] "Buddy"?

264
00:14:05,300 --> 00:14:06,600
Do you think
you're the same age?

265
00:14:06,600 --> 00:14:09,267
He's right, Ma. Gloria can pass
as your grandkid.

266
00:14:10,167 --> 00:14:12,833
[DIDAY] Then you make one
so I do have a grandchild!

267
00:14:12,833 --> 00:14:15,433
But then again,
you look your father.

268
00:14:15,433 --> 00:14:18,533
- You're both ugly. It's true.
- Ma!

269
00:14:20,133 --> 00:14:21,433
Buddy, what do you need?

270
00:14:21,433 --> 00:14:24,267
Gabo needs some formal clothes.

271
00:14:24,267 --> 00:14:26,800
I want to borrow it
for his job interview.

272
00:14:26,800 --> 00:14:29,267
- Gabo has an interview?
- Didn't you hear?

273
00:14:29,300 --> 00:14:31,167
He's getting interviewed
for a job!

274
00:14:32,967 --> 00:14:36,200
- Simang! Simang!
- What is it, Miss Diday?

275
00:14:36,200 --> 00:14:39,433
Do you have some formal clothes
for Gabo?

276
00:14:39,433 --> 00:14:41,367
Formal clothes for Gabo?

277
00:14:41,367 --> 00:14:43,333
- [DIDAY] Yes!
- I have one for ladies.

278
00:14:43,333 --> 00:14:45,033
What if I hit you, huh?

279
00:14:45,033 --> 00:14:46,267
- [ESTONG] Ma.
- Go!

280
00:14:46,267 --> 00:14:47,467
[ESTONG]
You're fighting everybody.

281
00:14:47,467 --> 00:14:51,600
Diday, just go with Gloria
to the thrift store.

282
00:14:51,600 --> 00:14:55,100
You'll have lots
of options there.

283
00:14:55,100 --> 00:14:57,200
That's actually my problem.

284
00:14:57,200 --> 00:14:59,333
I don't have money to buy any.

285
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:02,267
Why, Gloria?
Does Gabo not give you?

286
00:15:04,067 --> 00:15:05,333
No, it's not like that.

287
00:15:05,333 --> 00:15:07,200
I just don't really ask him
for money.

288
00:15:07,200 --> 00:15:09,133
I mean,
he pays for me, after all.

289
00:15:09,133 --> 00:15:11,667
Listen, if you want,
I can lend you some money.

290
00:15:11,667 --> 00:15:13,367
You can pay me anytime.

291
00:15:13,367 --> 00:15:16,300
Oh no, I don't want
to be a burden.

292
00:15:17,333 --> 00:15:19,467
I've got an idea.
Why don't we hustle a bit?

293
00:15:19,467 --> 00:15:21,400
We've still got time
before Gabo's interview.

294
00:15:21,400 --> 00:15:22,667
The problem is,

295
00:15:22,667 --> 00:15:25,500
Gabo doesn't want me going out

296
00:15:25,500 --> 00:15:27,067
after what happened last night.

297
00:15:27,067 --> 00:15:28,633
Don't worry.

298
00:15:28,633 --> 00:15:31,167
You won't get into any trouble
as long as I'm with you.

299
00:15:31,167 --> 00:15:32,333
I've got your back.

300
00:15:32,333 --> 00:15:34,467
[ESTONG]
Mama, she really can't leave.

301
00:15:34,900 --> 00:15:37,133
Bring me my magic bag.

302
00:15:37,567 --> 00:15:39,233
- What, the big one?
- Yes.

303
00:15:39,233 --> 00:15:41,033
[SILLY MUSIC PLAYING]

304
00:15:41,033 --> 00:15:42,000
Here, Mama.

305
00:15:44,233 --> 00:15:45,533
Look here.

306
00:15:45,533 --> 00:15:47,300
You'll believe in magic
once we make money with these.

307
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:50,067
Come on, let's get going now.

308
00:15:50,067 --> 00:15:51,033
Give me that.

309
00:15:51,033 --> 00:15:52,033
Hand it over.

310
00:15:52,033 --> 00:15:53,033
[CAP RUSTLING]

311
00:15:55,600 --> 00:15:56,933
Hurry, let's go!

312
00:15:56,933 --> 00:15:58,700
I know places where
we can make some money!

313
00:15:58,700 --> 00:16:00,000
Let's move!

314
00:16:00,433 --> 00:16:02,367
- Alright...
- [ESTONG] Stay safe, okay?

315
00:16:02,367 --> 00:16:03,533
- Be careful!
- I'll just fix it!

316
00:16:03,533 --> 00:16:04,933
Mama!

317
00:16:04,933 --> 00:16:06,167
You'd better take care
of Gloria!

318
00:16:06,167 --> 00:16:07,400
Gabo will have your head
if anything happens!

319
00:16:07,900 --> 00:16:09,000
[DIDAY] Come on!

320
00:16:10,100 --> 00:16:11,233
He's back.

321
00:16:12,100 --> 00:16:13,200
Boss Django.

322
00:16:13,633 --> 00:16:15,333
[OBJECT THUDDING]

323
00:16:15,400 --> 00:16:19,100
I saw Umali and his friend
here in Ginintuang Lupa.

324
00:16:19,100 --> 00:16:22,433
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

325
00:16:22,433 --> 00:16:24,200
Come on, let's check them out.

326
00:16:24,600 --> 00:16:26,433
I wonder what
they're doing here.

327
00:16:27,067 --> 00:16:28,400
What else?

328
00:16:28,400 --> 00:16:30,267
They're obviously looking
for the man from last night.

329
00:16:30,267 --> 00:16:31,433
- [GROANS]
- [CHUCKLING]

330
00:16:31,433 --> 00:16:33,733
What you mean is,
they're after you.

331
00:16:33,733 --> 00:16:35,967
[LAUGHTER]

332
00:16:35,967 --> 00:16:38,700
I'll make sure
they find Gabo instead.

333
00:16:38,700 --> 00:16:40,067
[LAUGHS]

334
00:16:40,067 --> 00:16:41,267
[GLASSES THUD]

335
00:16:41,300 --> 00:16:42,400
- Come on.
- Let's go.

336
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:47,167
[MUSIC BECOMES TENSE]

337
00:16:47,167 --> 00:16:48,433
[INDISTINCT CROWD CHATTER]

338
00:16:48,433 --> 00:16:51,100
Just don't mention what
happened at the safe house.

339
00:16:51,433 --> 00:16:53,433
They don't need to know
we're with the NLEA.

340
00:16:54,233 --> 00:16:55,267
What's my excuse?

341
00:16:55,267 --> 00:16:57,000
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER
IN DISTANCE]

342
00:16:57,000 --> 00:17:00,133
Tell them we're looking
for a friend.

343
00:17:00,667 --> 00:17:02,100
- Uh, ma'am?
- Hello.

344
00:17:02,100 --> 00:17:03,633
- Can I ask you a question?
- Sure thing.

345
00:17:03,633 --> 00:17:05,967
Did you notice anyone
on a motorbike around here?

346
00:17:05,967 --> 00:17:07,400
Look, there are loads
of them riding around here.

347
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:10,667
Someone who was speeding,
like they were in a rush.

348
00:17:10,667 --> 00:17:12,067
Young man, please.

349
00:17:12,067 --> 00:17:14,167
Everyone on a bike here is
always in a hurry.

350
00:17:14,167 --> 00:17:15,233
T-Thanks.

351
00:17:15,267 --> 00:17:17,100
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

352
00:17:17,100 --> 00:17:18,700
Hello, boss.

353
00:17:18,700 --> 00:17:20,733
- What's up?
- Can I ask you a question?

354
00:17:21,167 --> 00:17:24,133
My car got hit the other night.

355
00:17:24,133 --> 00:17:26,267
The guy on the motorbike
who crashed into me...

356
00:17:26,267 --> 00:17:28,800
People say
he's from around here.

357
00:17:28,800 --> 00:17:30,300
What kind of motorcycle?

358
00:17:30,300 --> 00:17:32,467
I'm not sure,
but here's a photo.

359
00:17:32,467 --> 00:17:34,067
- Let me see.
- What does it look like?

360
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:36,000
Ah.

361
00:17:36,533 --> 00:17:37,500
I know this one.

362
00:17:37,800 --> 00:17:39,500
- You do?
- Yes, that's right.

363
00:17:40,167 --> 00:17:41,300
Nice.

364
00:17:41,300 --> 00:17:42,467
Will you come with us?

365
00:17:42,467 --> 00:17:43,533
Just like that?

366
00:17:43,533 --> 00:17:46,033
At least give us
a little something.

367
00:17:46,033 --> 00:17:47,433
For drinks.

368
00:17:47,433 --> 00:17:49,200
- We're having a few right now.
- What do you say?

369
00:17:49,233 --> 00:17:50,367
Alright.

370
00:17:50,367 --> 00:17:52,333
You'll come with me,
point out the suspect,

371
00:17:52,333 --> 00:17:53,667
and I'll give you
five hundred pesos.

372
00:17:53,667 --> 00:17:55,067
- Sounds good?
- It's a deal!

373
00:17:55,067 --> 00:17:57,033
Come on, follow me!

374
00:17:57,033 --> 00:17:58,200
This way!

375
00:17:58,200 --> 00:17:59,733
Hurry, let's go!

376
00:17:59,733 --> 00:18:01,733
[MUSIC SWELLING]

377
00:18:01,733 --> 00:18:02,833
[MUSIC FADES]

378
00:18:02,833 --> 00:18:05,333
Sir, is this
your first time here?

379
00:18:05,333 --> 00:18:07,467
I've never seen you
around these parts before.

380
00:18:07,467 --> 00:18:09,400
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

381
00:18:09,400 --> 00:18:11,467
Don't worry,
I'll make your face real smooth.

382
00:18:11,467 --> 00:18:12,500
[CUSTOMER YELPS]

383
00:18:12,500 --> 00:18:14,533
- Please, be gentle!
- Oh, come on!

384
00:18:15,133 --> 00:18:16,800
- I'm being gentle right now!
- You're hurting me!

385
00:18:17,400 --> 00:18:19,367
This will make you handsome.

386
00:18:19,367 --> 00:18:22,533
- I look like a corpse.
- Of course not! I've got you!

387
00:18:22,567 --> 00:18:24,400
Just relax, okay?

388
00:18:24,400 --> 00:18:26,533
- How can I relax right now?
- [NECK SNAPS]

389
00:18:26,533 --> 00:18:28,700
- Look, I've got you.
- [NECK SNAPS]

390
00:18:28,700 --> 00:18:30,733
I know what I'm doing.
How do you feel now?

391
00:18:30,733 --> 00:18:32,533
I told you
it's going to be fine!

392
00:18:32,533 --> 00:18:33,867
See?

393
00:18:33,867 --> 00:18:35,700
- I'm never coming back here!
- [SARCASTICALLY] Wow.

394
00:18:35,700 --> 00:18:37,367
You're the one complaining, huh?

395
00:18:37,367 --> 00:18:38,633
Jeez.

396
00:18:40,667 --> 00:18:41,700
Hey, you.

397
00:18:41,700 --> 00:18:43,167
- I'll get a haircut next time.
- No.

398
00:18:43,167 --> 00:18:45,433
- You're in line, right? Hey!
- I'll come back next time.

399
00:18:45,433 --> 00:18:46,800
- Hey! Hey!
- I'll get a haircut next time.

400
00:18:47,400 --> 00:18:48,500
That man...

401
00:18:48,500 --> 00:18:51,500
Uh, sir.
I would like to get a haircut.

402
00:18:51,500 --> 00:18:54,467
Okay. Sit here. Sit.

403
00:18:56,200 --> 00:18:57,067
[SIGHS DEEPLY]

404
00:18:58,700 --> 00:19:00,200
Alright.

405
00:19:00,200 --> 00:19:05,700
Uh, sir, I'd like to get
the military cut.

406
00:19:05,700 --> 00:19:07,667
Alright. I'll take care of it.

407
00:19:08,067 --> 00:19:09,400
I'll make you handsome.

408
00:19:10,400 --> 00:19:15,633
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

409
00:19:15,633 --> 00:19:16,667
[MAN] There, sir!

410
00:19:19,400 --> 00:19:20,533
- Get him!
- [SANTOS] Stop.

411
00:19:20,533 --> 00:19:21,567
- Oh.
- Why?

412
00:19:22,933 --> 00:19:24,667
Come here, come here.

413
00:19:25,933 --> 00:19:27,000
Where were you last night?

414
00:19:27,567 --> 00:19:29,400
I was out on a delivery.

415
00:19:29,433 --> 00:19:31,867
- What's your job?
- I'm a delivery rider.

416
00:19:34,133 --> 00:19:36,733
- What time did you get home?
- Around 11 in the evening.

417
00:19:36,733 --> 00:19:39,633
Where were you
from 9 to 10 o'clock?

418
00:19:39,633 --> 00:19:42,133
I was out doing deliveries.
Here's proof.

419
00:19:43,567 --> 00:19:44,633
Check it.

420
00:19:44,633 --> 00:19:46,067
[MAN] Those are
my job orders last night.

421
00:19:51,900 --> 00:19:52,867
Give it back.

422
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:55,067
You're wrong.

423
00:19:58,100 --> 00:19:59,967
[DIDAY] Come, Gloria.

424
00:19:59,967 --> 00:20:03,533
I've got a lot of regulars here
for manicures and pedicures.

425
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:05,267
- Manicure and pedicure?
- Yeah!

426
00:20:05,267 --> 00:20:07,600
But I don't know
how to clean someone's nails.

427
00:20:07,600 --> 00:20:09,567
I'll take care of you!

428
00:20:10,667 --> 00:20:12,033
- Are you sure?
- Yeah!

429
00:20:12,033 --> 00:20:15,933
You know, I can clean
even a carabao's nails.

430
00:20:15,933 --> 00:20:19,100
- Take care!
- [DIDAY] Hey, Bebang!

431
00:20:19,100 --> 00:20:22,000
You're so beautiful today!
Your cheeks are so red!

432
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:25,167
- You're all dolled up!
- Not really. [GIGGLES]

433
00:20:25,167 --> 00:20:26,833
I just washed my face
with water.

434
00:20:26,833 --> 00:20:29,167
But what if I used soap too?
[GIGGLES]

435
00:20:30,700 --> 00:20:32,000
No, it's true!

436
00:20:32,667 --> 00:20:34,600
You're so beautiful today,
you're practically glowing!

437
00:20:34,600 --> 00:20:37,267
You guys!
Why are you here, anyway?

438
00:20:37,300 --> 00:20:40,100
What else? Are you going
to get your nails cleaned?

439
00:20:42,133 --> 00:20:43,800
Why not?

440
00:20:43,867 --> 00:20:46,133
Well, what can I do
when you're already here?

441
00:20:46,133 --> 00:20:48,133
I mean, look at your big body.

442
00:20:48,133 --> 00:20:49,300
Come, let's get inside.

443
00:20:49,300 --> 00:20:51,967
I want a french tip
with some rhinestones.

444
00:20:51,967 --> 00:20:54,967
Come on, let's get inside.
Hurry up!

445
00:20:56,167 --> 00:20:57,133
Come!

446
00:20:59,833 --> 00:21:02,700
It's good you decided to get
a haircut, Gabo.

447
00:21:02,700 --> 00:21:04,633
Your hair's been long
for a while now.

448
00:21:04,633 --> 00:21:05,967
[GABO CHUCKLES]

449
00:21:05,967 --> 00:21:09,633
I didn't actually want
to get a haircut, but my wife...

450
00:21:10,333 --> 00:21:13,700
She told me to get a haircut
'cause I'll apply for jobs.

451
00:21:13,700 --> 00:21:15,733
I'll take care of you!

452
00:21:15,733 --> 00:21:17,767
You know, we have a promo today!

453
00:21:17,767 --> 00:21:19,167
It's just like
an electric chair.

454
00:21:19,167 --> 00:21:21,700
The cut's a lot cleaner
than a clean cut!

455
00:21:21,700 --> 00:21:23,100
You should go bald!

456
00:21:23,100 --> 00:21:24,167
[GABO CHUCKLES]

457
00:21:24,167 --> 00:21:25,667
I'd rather not, sir.

458
00:21:25,667 --> 00:21:27,767
I've kept this hair
for a long time.

459
00:21:27,767 --> 00:21:29,933
I'd rather go
for the military cut.

460
00:21:29,933 --> 00:21:31,100
It's what my wife wants.

461
00:21:31,100 --> 00:21:32,833
So you think
you know better than me?

462
00:21:32,833 --> 00:21:34,800
Are you the barber? Huh?

463
00:21:35,600 --> 00:21:36,800
[KNIFE SWISHING]

464
00:21:38,067 --> 00:21:40,533
Will you just scare me,
or will you cut my hair?

465
00:21:40,533 --> 00:21:42,700
Want me to pierce a hole
through your neck? Huh?!

466
00:21:42,733 --> 00:21:47,033
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

467
00:21:47,033 --> 00:21:48,767
You think you know better
than me, huh?

468
00:21:48,767 --> 00:21:50,700
- [MURMURING]
- Fix my haircut!

469
00:21:51,133 --> 00:21:52,967
Or else I'm going to slice
your neck!

470
00:21:52,967 --> 00:21:54,000
Gabo, don't.

471
00:21:54,700 --> 00:21:57,600
- Do it properly!
- I will. I am!

472
00:21:57,600 --> 00:21:59,867
- Why are you shaking?
- I'm not.

473
00:21:59,867 --> 00:22:04,100
But, o-of course,
y-you put out y-your...

474
00:22:05,967 --> 00:22:07,267
...knife!

475
00:22:07,267 --> 00:22:10,333
I was just joking earlier,
G-Gabo.

476
00:22:11,700 --> 00:22:13,767
- Do it properly.
- I will.

477
00:22:14,367 --> 00:22:15,867
[LALA] Clean it properly.

478
00:22:15,900 --> 00:22:19,667
[UMALI] I told you.
It smells in here.

479
00:22:19,667 --> 00:22:21,600
[SANTOS]
We can't even find the guy.

480
00:22:21,600 --> 00:22:22,900
[UMALI] How annoying.

481
00:22:22,900 --> 00:22:24,400
Hello, handsome!

482
00:22:24,400 --> 00:22:26,400
It's good you visited!

483
00:22:26,400 --> 00:22:29,233
We're doing some service.
Want me to serve you?

484
00:22:29,233 --> 00:22:32,267
I mean, I have a parlor.
Maybe you want to get a hair--

485
00:22:34,233 --> 00:22:37,633
Want to get a haircut?
I'll give it to you for free.

486
00:22:37,633 --> 00:22:40,933
Ah, no. We're actually looking
for someone with a motorcycle.

487
00:22:42,133 --> 00:22:44,400
Well, there's lots of those
in here.

488
00:22:44,400 --> 00:22:47,100
In fact, I know some of them.

489
00:22:47,100 --> 00:22:48,600
What do they look like?

490
00:22:48,600 --> 00:22:50,800
- They have long hair.
- Long hair?

491
00:22:51,767 --> 00:22:52,900
There, she has long hair.

492
00:22:53,767 --> 00:22:55,000
Just kidding!

493
00:22:55,000 --> 00:22:58,833
I meant, are they thin, slim,
fat, brown-skinned,

494
00:22:58,833 --> 00:23:01,167
- or fair-skinned like me?
- He's a man.

495
00:23:01,933 --> 00:23:03,167
A man? Hmm...

496
00:23:03,933 --> 00:23:06,100
- There's no one.
- Alright.

497
00:23:06,100 --> 00:23:09,000
If you see a man with long hair
riding a motorcycle...

498
00:23:09,767 --> 00:23:11,267
I'll come to you.
Where's your parlor shop?

499
00:23:11,267 --> 00:23:14,133
Yes, go to my parlor!
I'll give you a discount.

500
00:23:14,133 --> 00:23:16,700
It's just over there,
near the arch.

501
00:23:16,700 --> 00:23:18,100
- Okay.
- Oh!

502
00:23:18,100 --> 00:23:23,000
Oh my god, Django,
you're here!

503
00:23:23,033 --> 00:23:25,467
Wait. Where's the long wig
you borrowed from me?

504
00:23:25,467 --> 00:23:27,800
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

505
00:23:27,800 --> 00:23:28,833
Long wig?

506
00:23:30,467 --> 00:23:35,400
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

507
00:23:35,400 --> 00:23:39,633
Ah, it's with my girlfriend.
She's at BeerGin.

508
00:23:40,300 --> 00:23:42,367
How much is it?
I'll just pay for it.

509
00:23:43,667 --> 00:23:44,767
Girlfriend?

510
00:23:45,900 --> 00:23:47,967
I thought I was your only one?

511
00:23:47,967 --> 00:23:50,800
I won't let this be.
You'll pay twice the amount!

512
00:23:50,800 --> 00:23:52,467
That's real hair.
That person is still alive--

513
00:23:52,467 --> 00:23:54,767
I'll pay for it.
Now leave.

514
00:23:55,833 --> 00:23:58,000
- Sister, where are you going?!
- Finish that.

515
00:23:58,000 --> 00:23:59,833
[GROANS]

516
00:24:01,333 --> 00:24:04,767
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

517
00:24:04,767 --> 00:24:05,733
So?

518
00:24:06,367 --> 00:24:08,333
Found what you're looking for?

519
00:24:08,333 --> 00:24:09,300
[UMALI CHUCKLES]

520
00:24:10,900 --> 00:24:12,333
Not yet.

521
00:24:12,333 --> 00:24:16,100
Didn't you say you were
looking for a long-haired man?

522
00:24:16,100 --> 00:24:18,367
We're looking for someone
who has long hair, curly hair,

523
00:24:18,367 --> 00:24:20,500
no hair, with or without teeth,

524
00:24:20,500 --> 00:24:22,800
so long as he has a motorcycle.

525
00:24:23,433 --> 00:24:25,400
Didn't you see his face
on the CCTV?

526
00:24:25,400 --> 00:24:26,467
There was nothing.

527
00:24:28,067 --> 00:24:31,200
There was no CCTV,
or you saw nothing?

528
00:24:31,233 --> 00:24:33,533
[UMALI CHUCKLES, INHALES]

529
00:24:33,533 --> 00:24:37,000
The CCTV cameras were damaged.
Others were covered.

530
00:24:38,400 --> 00:24:40,867
You didn't see anything?
Not even one?

531
00:24:40,867 --> 00:24:42,000
They're still fixing it.

532
00:24:43,067 --> 00:24:44,433
Well.

533
00:24:44,533 --> 00:24:47,133
We'll tell you
once we see his profile.

534
00:24:47,133 --> 00:24:48,100
[DJANGO EXHALES]

535
00:24:48,733 --> 00:24:49,900
Too bad.

536
00:24:49,900 --> 00:24:52,733
Like I told you,
show me his photo,

537
00:24:52,733 --> 00:24:54,433
and I'll find him myself.

538
00:24:54,433 --> 00:24:55,400
Okay.

539
00:24:56,433 --> 00:24:57,367
If that's what you say.

540
00:24:59,900 --> 00:25:01,867
So long as
he's from Ginintuang Lupa,

541
00:25:01,900 --> 00:25:04,033
I'll eventually find him.

542
00:25:04,467 --> 00:25:06,067
This is my territory.

543
00:25:07,067 --> 00:25:08,467
I'll take your word
for it, Django.

544
00:25:10,067 --> 00:25:16,967
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

545
00:25:24,733 --> 00:25:25,733
Sir.

546
00:25:26,567 --> 00:25:27,533
Sir.

547
00:25:28,567 --> 00:25:29,900
Why didn't we tell Django

548
00:25:29,900 --> 00:25:31,933
about the long-haired man
we're looking for?

549
00:25:32,667 --> 00:25:36,067
Our search could've been easier
with his help.

550
00:25:36,867 --> 00:25:37,900
And then what?

551
00:25:39,533 --> 00:25:40,733
I know Django.

552
00:25:41,533 --> 00:25:45,167
If he realizes
we're looking for gold,

553
00:25:45,167 --> 00:25:46,633
he'll start meddling.

554
00:25:47,133 --> 00:25:48,067
Besides...

555
00:25:48,767 --> 00:25:50,733
I still have my suspicions.

556
00:25:51,500 --> 00:25:54,667
He's the one who ambushed NLEA,
and trespassed the safe house.

557
00:25:54,667 --> 00:25:56,733
You're right, sir.

558
00:25:57,600 --> 00:25:58,933
It'd be better
if he doesn't know.

559
00:26:01,467 --> 00:26:02,767
For now, let's look for that

560
00:26:02,767 --> 00:26:04,167
long-haired jerk
on a motorcycle.

561
00:26:04,833 --> 00:26:06,733
And then we deal with Django.

562
00:26:10,567 --> 00:26:12,967
NLEA really is useless.

563
00:26:12,967 --> 00:26:16,167
I already made it easy for them,
and they still can't catch him.

564
00:26:16,167 --> 00:26:17,767
They have to catch Gabo!

565
00:26:18,633 --> 00:26:20,500
Is it true
there's no CCTV recording?

566
00:26:20,500 --> 00:26:21,867
Did we cover them all
last night?

567
00:26:22,700 --> 00:26:23,667
Of course not!

568
00:26:24,133 --> 00:26:25,967
You know, I made an effort.

569
00:26:27,300 --> 00:26:30,700
I even wore a wig,
so they'd think I was Gabo.

570
00:26:31,300 --> 00:26:33,600
Maybe they're just not saying
that they've found him.

571
00:26:35,233 --> 00:26:36,200
I think...

572
00:26:37,300 --> 00:26:38,800
...they're playing
their own game.

573
00:26:40,133 --> 00:26:42,500
But I don't care
what they're up to.

574
00:26:43,000 --> 00:26:46,500
They need to get to Gabo.
If they do...

575
00:26:47,833 --> 00:26:49,133
He'll end up in prison again.

576
00:26:50,667 --> 00:26:52,833
And Gloria will be mine.

577
00:26:52,833 --> 00:26:55,867
[DJANGO CHUCKLING]

578
00:26:57,167 --> 00:26:59,000
Hey, Estong. Where's Gabo?

579
00:26:59,833 --> 00:27:02,267
Over there.
Getting a haircut.

580
00:27:02,267 --> 00:27:04,167
What?! He's getting a haircut?!

581
00:27:04,167 --> 00:27:06,633
Hey, what you're saying
is impossible.

582
00:27:07,067 --> 00:27:08,667
Yeah, that's impossible!

583
00:27:08,667 --> 00:27:11,600
Gabo never let others touch
his hair even when we were kids.

584
00:27:11,600 --> 00:27:13,200
I'm the only one
who can touch his hair.

585
00:27:13,200 --> 00:27:14,767
And you're telling me
he's getting a haircut?

586
00:27:14,767 --> 00:27:17,000
Gloria told him
to get a haircut.

587
00:27:17,033 --> 00:27:20,200
He's getting a haircut
all because Gloria said so?

588
00:27:20,200 --> 00:27:23,567
[IN UNISON] That just means
he's whipped!

589
00:27:23,567 --> 00:27:25,367
[TEKLA] Wait, this can't be.
This can't be!

590
00:27:25,367 --> 00:27:28,367
- I'll talk him out of it.
- Hey, hey, Tekla!

591
00:27:28,367 --> 00:27:31,200
Gabo! Hey, sir, stop!

592
00:27:31,200 --> 00:27:35,833
Don't! Gabo, why are you getting
a haircut?

593
00:27:38,100 --> 00:27:40,800
- Gloria wants me to.
- What?!

594
00:27:40,800 --> 00:27:43,733
She said I should get a haircut
before I apply for a job.

595
00:27:43,733 --> 00:27:44,867
[TEKLA] What?!

596
00:27:44,867 --> 00:27:47,733
All because that
fair-skinned fish said so?!

597
00:27:47,733 --> 00:27:49,067
Don't get a haircut, Gabo.

598
00:27:49,100 --> 00:27:51,067
You look so handsome
with long hair.

599
00:27:51,067 --> 00:27:52,733
You look like Adonis.

600
00:27:52,733 --> 00:27:54,167
[CHEERING]

601
00:27:54,167 --> 00:27:56,800
[TOLITS] Tekla, let him be.
That's what his wife said.

602
00:27:56,800 --> 00:27:58,333
Wife?!

603
00:27:58,333 --> 00:28:00,400
Who knows, maybe Gabo is
more handsome with short hair.

604
00:28:00,400 --> 00:28:02,067
No, I don't like that!

605
00:28:02,067 --> 00:28:04,400
[IPE]
Our friend has really changed.

606
00:28:04,400 --> 00:28:05,633
He's wrapped around her thumb.

607
00:28:05,633 --> 00:28:08,100
[CHUCKLING, SCREAMING]

608
00:28:08,100 --> 00:28:09,267
I don't fold.

609
00:28:11,167 --> 00:28:12,633
I just love.

610
00:28:12,633 --> 00:28:16,333
[SCREAMING]

611
00:28:16,333 --> 00:28:23,300
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

612
00:28:26,433 --> 00:28:28,833
<i>We came here to talk
to Gen. Jacinto.</i>

613
00:28:28,833 --> 00:28:30,433
<i> Get out of my property.</i>

614
00:28:30,433 --> 00:28:32,267
<i>Why did Samantha die?
Who is to blame?</i>

615
00:28:32,267 --> 00:28:34,467
<i>Don't ever mention
my daughter's name!</i>

616
00:28:34,467 --> 00:28:35,600
<i> How dare you even ask that!</i>

617
00:28:35,600 --> 00:28:37,500
<i>Even though she is now
in the afterlife,</i>

618
00:28:37,500 --> 00:28:40,800
<i>she still cares
about our safety.</i>

619
00:28:40,800 --> 00:28:45,333
<i>- I'm your mommy, Sam!
- Mommy!</i>

620
00:28:45,333 --> 00:28:47,433
<i>Gabo! Those men last night
came back!</i>

621
00:28:48,833 --> 00:28:50,967
<i>You've got a lot of nerve
coming back here!</i>

622
00:28:50,967 --> 00:28:52,933
<i>But now, you're not getting
out of here alive!</i>
